  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nA boundary will continue to work through the region overnight. While\nprecipitation is not expected, there will be a wind shift. High \ntemperatures today will generally be in the 70s with a few 80s \npossible south of the Ohio River. On Friday the Tri-State will see \n80s while central Ohio will be in the lower to middle 70s. For the \nday on Saturday, temperatures will generally be in the 70s with a few\n80 degrees also possible. Temperatures overnight will be in the 40s \nand 50s.\n\nKey Message 2)\n\nThe remnants from Hurricane Isaias will move into the region late \nSaturday through Sunday. Most of the rain will hold off during the \ndaytime hours on Saturday and move into the region during the \nevening and overnight hours. Rain will be widespread and continue \nduring the day on Sunday before tapering off Sunday night. Dry \nconditions are expected for Monday. Breezy conditions are expected \nSaturday evening through Sunday. At this time NBM has wind gusts up \nto near 30 mph, however some higher wind gusts around 40 mph will \nlikely occur. Did not make any changes to wind gusts at this time,\nhowever depending on the exact track, they will likely need to be\nincreased with time. Lowered temperatures this weekend, however \ntemperatures will likely need some additional lowering as details \nresolve.\n\nKey Message 3)\n\nA quick moving system will move through on Tuesday bringing with it\nsome showers for Tuesday and cooler air for Wednesday. At this time,\nlows look to be in the 40s and therefore do not expect frost.",
